 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+### 2Q Eviction Strategy
+
+Cache replacement uses the 2Q algorithm to protect comparison sheets from being flushed by sequential screenings:
+- **A1in (FIFO queue)**: Newly rendered contact sheets are first admitted into `A1in`. If an item in `A1in` is referenced again while still in `A1in`, it is promoted directly to `Am`.
+- **A1out (FIFO ghost cache / metadata queue)**: When `A1in` exceeds its quota, entries are evicted from disk; their keys are tracked in `A1out` (storing metadata/keys only, no JPEG bytes).
+- **Am (LRU queue)**: Long-term hot entries live in `Am`. If a requested preview is not cached on disk but its key hits in `A1out`, upon render completion it is admitted directly into `Am`. If an entry in `Am` is hit, it is moved to the head of `Am`.
+- **Eviction target**: When disk space is required to admit a sheet, evict from `A1in` first if its size exceeds its threshold; otherwise evict the tail of `Am`.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Cache eviction policy | 2Q (Two-Queue) | LRU, Frequency-based eviction with aging | Protects frequently revisited comparison sheets from being evicted during long sequential screening scans, without the counter maintenance and project-switch lag of frequency aging. |
+
+## Open Questions & Future Decisions
+
+### Resolved
+1. Eviction policy: 2Q selected to protect comparison sheets against scan pollution.
+
+### Deferred
+1. Concrete capacity and size split ratio between `A1` and `Am` (e.g., 25% A1in / 75% Am) to be tuned based on production screening metrics.
